course: dictionary
lesson: 13423
title: Hm: the thinking sound
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Hm» is not a word with a meaning you can look up like «happy». It is a sound people make, and it is written as hm, hmm or hmmm. Each spelling sounds much the same.
explain: People use it when they are thinking, not sure, or doubtful. «Hm, let me think about that.» The speaker is buying time to think before they answer.
explain: The same sound can also show you are not convinced. «Hmm, are you sure?» means the speaker has doubts. Look at the rest of the sentence and the face or voice to know which feeling it is.
fact: Hm, hmm and hmmm are all ways of writing the same thinking sound.
fact: In stories and comics, «Hmm» shows a character is thinking, puzzled or doubtful.
fact: When you speak, «Hm» gives you time to think before you answer.
fact: Teachers may say «Hmm» to mean, check your answer again.
fact: In texting, «hm» can sound doubtful or unimpressed, so think about how it might be read.
exercise: «Hm, let me think.» What is the speaker doing? | Laughing at a joke | Going to sleep | *Thinking before answering | Shouting for help
exercise: «Hmm, are you sure?» What does the speaker feel? | Angry and crying | *Doubt, not fully convinced | Very sleepy | Excited and cheering
exercise: In a comic, a character rubs her chin and says «Hmmm». What is she showing? | She is starting a song | She has finished the book | She is hungry | *She is puzzled or working something out
test: Your teacher says «Hmm» after your answer. What might it mean? | You have won the prize | *Check your answer again | The lesson is over | Sit down and be quiet forever
test: A friend texts «hm» after you show them your drawing. Which reply fits the way «hm» can sound? | Wow, amazing, thank you! | *Hm. Okay, whatever. | Haha, love it! | Yay, see you soon!
exam: «Hm, I suppose that could work.» What does «hm» show here? | Angry and shouting | Happy with the idea | Asleep | *Not fully convinced, a bit doubtful
